 "script": [
  {"id": "hook", "text": "Putin just agreed to talk again. Will this round be any different?"},
  {"id": "f1", "text": "On Wednesday in Saint Petersburg, U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff met Vladimir Putin for about three hours. The Kremlin says Putin agreed in principle to resume three-way talks with Washington and Kyiv. A day earlier, Witkoff met Zelenskyy and European leaders in Oslo."},
  {"id": "f2", "text": "Kremlin aide Yuri Ushakov says the talks could come after November tenth, possibly in Abu Dhabi. No date is confirmed. Zelenskyy wants talks by early November. Russia also freed an American teacher, Stephen Hubbard."},
  {"id": "f3", "text": "But Ushakov said the ideas from Oslo had little substance. Foreign Policy reports Moscow has not moved on Donetsk or on Ukraine joining NATO. AP sees no sign of a high-level breakthrough. Both sides strike daily. Ukraine says it will hit Russian energy sites as long as Russia hits its own."},
  {"id": "cta", "text": "Will Russia and Ukraine sit down before December? Yes or no?"}
 ],
