  "title": "Putin Agrees to Talks. Will Anything Change? #shorts",
  "description": "After a three-hour meeting with U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff in St. Petersburg on October 21, the Kremlin says Putin agreed in principle to resume three-way talks with the U.S. and Ukraine. Kremlin aide Yuri Ushakov said they could take place after November 10, possibly in Abu Dhabi; no date is confirmed. Zelenskyy wants talks by early November. Russia also released American teacher Stephen Hubbard. Foreign Policy reports Moscow has not signaled compromise on Donetsk or NATO, and AP sees no sign of an imminent high-level breakthrough.\n\nSources:\nPBS NewsHour / AP: Putin agrees to resume trilateral Russia-Ukraine-U.S. talks next month (Oct 21, 2026)\nAl Jazeera: Putin and Zelenskyy back three-way US peace talks on Ukraine (Oct 21, 2026)\nAxios: Putin tells Witkoff he is ready to resume direct peace talks (Oct 21, 2026)\nForeign Policy: Witkoff pushes Putin to restart Russia-Ukraine peace talks (Oct 21, 2026)\nABC News (Australia): Putin agrees to resume three-way talks on Ukraine war (Oct 22, 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #Russia #PeaceTalks",
